NNAAMMEE
     mmkkffiiffoo — make fifos

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmkkffiiffoo [--mm _m_o_d_e] _f_i_f_o___n_a_m_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmkkffiiffoo utility creates the fifos requested, in the order specified.

     The options are as follows:

     --mm      Set the file permission bits of the created fifos to the speci‐
             fied mode, ignoring the umask(2) of the calling process.  The
             _m_o_d_e argument takes any format that can be specified to the
             chmod(1) command.  If a symbolic mode is specified, the op sym‐
             bols ‘+’ (plus) and ‘-’ (hyphen) are interpreted relative to an
             assumed initial mode of “a=rw” (read and write permissions for
             all).

     If the --mm option is not specified, fifos are created with mode 0666 modi‐
     fied by the umask(2) of the calling process.  The mmkkffiiffoo utility requires
     write permission in the parent directory.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The mmkkffiiffoo utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     mkdir(1), rm(1), mkfifo(2), mknod(2), mknod(8)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The mmkkffiiffoo utility is expected to be IEEE Std 1003.2 (“POSIX.2”) compli‐
     ant.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The mmkkffiiffoo command appeared in 4.4BSD.

